<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  BRAINWORM_MOD_BUILD_1. Attaches RSW_RemoveBrainWorm to every race that can be
  operated on at all.

  Vanilla attaches surgeries like ExciseCarcinoma through each race ThingDef's own
  <recipes> list, not through RecipeDef.recipeUsers - so "already lists
  ExciseCarcinoma" is the reliable marker for "this is a body a surgeon works on".
  Patches run against the raw XML BEFORE def inheritance resolves, so matching the
  two defs that DECLARE that list - Human (Races_Humanlike.xml) and the abstract
  AnimalThingBase (Races_Animal_Base.xml) - reaches every vanilla race through
  inheritance, and reaches any alien race in the load order that copied the vanilla
  list rather than inheriting it.

  Animals match too. Harmless: CompRSWWormBurrow refuses a non-Humanlike host, so
  an animal never carries the hediff, and Recipe_RemoveHediff.AvailableOnNow
  returns false when the hediff is absent - the bill never appears.

  ⚠️ A patch that matches nothing logs nothing. If the extract-brain-worm bill is
  missing from a race's operations tab, this xpath found no <recipes> on it; add
  that race explicitly rather than assuming the patch ran.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationAdd">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[recipes/li="ExciseCarcinoma"]/recipes</xpath>
    <value>
      <li>RSW_RemoveBrainWorm</li>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
